            <ArticleTitle>Deep Transverse Metacarpal Ligament Reconstruction Using Suture Button and A1 Pulley.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>128-130</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1097/BTH.0000000000000169</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Rupture of the deep transverse metacarpal ligament (DTML) can result in pain, impaired grip strength, and undermine functional performance of the hand. We describe the case of a patient whose right hand came into contact with a boat propeller. He sustained a complete disruption of the DTML between the second and third ray in addition to soft tissue injury and open metacarpal fractures. Although other techniques describe a reconstruction of the DTML, our technique describes an adjunctive technique that strongly augments the A1 pulley reconstruction and nullifies the requirements of palmaris longus graft.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
